# REFERENCES, NOT VALUES — which is why this file is committed.
#
# `op run --env-file=.env.op -- <command>` resolves each `op://` line against 1Password and
# hands the command the secret in its environment, so no Strava credential is ever written to
# disk in this repository or pasted into a shell. Nothing here is secret: an `op://` reference
# is an address, and reading it needs an authenticated 1Password session that this file cannot
# supply.
#
# `.gitignore` IGNORES `.env*` AND THEN NEGATES THIS FILE BY NAME, so it is committed on
# purpose rather than by omission. The wildcard is deliberate and this file's header used to
# argue against it: the exact-name list it replaced missed the five filenames Astro and Vite's
# own `.env.[mode]` convention produces.
#
# WHAT THE NEGATION ACTUALLY DOES, stated carefully because the obvious reading is wrong: an
# ignore rule has NO EFFECT ON A TRACKED FILE, so deleting `!.env.op` would not un-commit or
# hide this one. What it protects is the NEXT add — a fresh clone that re-creates the file, a
# rename, a second reference file — which the `.env*` wildcard would otherwise refuse, quietly
# turning the credential path undiscoverable again. That is what plan 022 was written to end.
# Keep the exception; do not go back to naming the ignored files instead.
#
#     op run --env-file=.env.op -- pnpm race:add 12058884605 12058885236
#     op run --env-file=.env.op -- pnpm strava:sync
#     op run --env-file=.env.op -- env STRAVA_VERIFY=1 pnpm vitest run tests/strava-verify.test.ts
#
# THE THREE CREDENTIALS, UNDER THE NAMES CI ALREADY USES. `scripts/strava-auth.mjs` reads
# exactly these, so the local path and the workflow path are one code path rather than two
# that happen to agree. The client secret is stored on the 1Password item's `credential`
# field, which is that item's own naming, not this repository's.
STRAVA_CLIENT_ID="op://Personal/calvindotsg-strava/client_id"
STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET="op://Personal/calvindotsg-strava/credential"
STRAVA_REFRESH_TOKEN="op://Personal/calvindotsg-strava/refresh_token"

# WHERE THE TRUTH LIVES AND WHERE THE COPY GOES. Plain values rather than references — they
# are addresses of an item and of a repository, both already public in README.md — and they
# are read only on the two paths that WRITE a credential: `pnpm strava:sync`, and the rotation
# branch in `scripts/strava-auth.mjs`. A process that lacks them cannot persist a rotation,
# which is the correct behaviour in CI and is why they are supplied here and nowhere else.
STRAVA_OP_VAULT="Personal"
STRAVA_OP_ITEM="calvindotsg-strava"
STRAVA_SECRET_REPO="calvindotsg/portfolio-v2"
